messages:
ana: Heads-up — onboarding teams keep hitting opaque errors from our SDKs. JS returns new Error(\"request failed\") with no code/status; Python wraps too generically. We should provide typed exceptions + clear status/code mapping. cc @michael @kate

michael: Agreed. Server actually returns structured JSON (e.g., {error: {type: 'rate_limit', message: '...'}}) but the JS SDK strips it and surfaces a plain Error. Hit this with customer-42.

kate: +1. Proposal: expose both HTTP status and a canonical error_code on every SDK error. Make a base RedwoodError with .status, .code, .details and then subclasses for common cases: AuthenticationError (401/403), RateLimitError (429), ValidationError (400), ModelError (5xx + model codes), NetworkError (timeouts/socket errors).

samir: Compatibility question — lots of users do cheap string-matching on message text. How do we avoid breaking them?

ana (typo correction): ana: (ignore previous) We should be non-breaking initially: add properties (code/status/details) to the Error object while keeping the message the same. Then introduce subclassed exceptions in a future major release. Also publish a migration note.

michael: Example TS sketch (for the thread):
```ts
export class RedwoodError extends Error {
  code?: string;
  status?: number;
  details?: any;
  constructor(message: string, code?: string, status?: number, details?: any) {
    super(message);
    this.code = code;
    this.status = status;
    this.details = details;
  }
}
export class RateLimitError extends RedwoodError {}
```

kate: Python sketch:
```py
class RedwoodError(Exception):
    def __init__(self, message, code=None, status=None, details=None):
        super().__init__(message)
        self.code = code
        self.status = status
        self.details = details
class RateLimitError(RedwoodError):
    pass
```

samir: Also we need a canonical mapping table in docs — e.g. 401 -> auth.invalid_credentials, 429 -> rate_limit.quota_exceeded, 400 -> validation.invalid_field, 422 -> validation.unprocessable, 503 -> server.unavailable. That will make sample apps stable.

michael: Agree — add the table and examples showing how to check errors safely: prefer `if (err.code === 'rate_limit.quota_exceeded')` over string.includes.

samir: Our reference sample app broke because it looked for the substring \"quota exceeded\". I'll open PRs to switch to code-based checks.

ci-bot: deploy-notice: sample-apps/service-a updated to use code checks — CI passed.

ana (again typo): ana: Action items:
- ana: open RFC issue listing proposed canonical codes + mapping table
- michael: draft JS PR adding code/status/details (non-breaking)
- kate: add Python patch mirroring fields, keep class names stable for now
- samir: update sample apps & tests to check .code instead of message text

Target: land additive fields in next minor (v2.4.0), introduce subclasses in v3.0 (breaking). We'll add deprecation notes and a migration guide. :thumbsup:
